-- Where legalese/l4-ide#804's slot and operand brackets meet what unstable has
-- and main does not. The l4-cli-test block "l4 render and nlg where #804 meets
-- unstable" reads each row.
--
-- 1. A mixfix call's hole. The port brackets every hole that does not read as
--    one thing, first, middle or last (5e2b00e4e). A mixfix call that ends with
--    a hole ends as the argument there does (#804's callEndsOpen), so in a
--    sentence's slot that the sentence goes on after it is bracketed whole
--    (`beats then shown` against `shown in a hole`). A call with one argument
--    reads as one thing in a hole, even one that ends with a condition, so
--    `one` and `two` still read alike (a stated limit). A mixfix call that is an
--    operand of arithmetic is bracketed as a whole (`sum then reduced`).
-- 2. unstable's ledger write, ledger read and refusal end in a clause of their
--    own ("100, recorded as balance"), so they take #804's brackets as an
--    operand of arithmetic and in a slot that the sentence goes on after. Each
--    pair below records or returns a different value and read alike before.

IMPORT prelude

GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fb` p IF p

GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN
@nlg %x% is shown
DECIDE `shown` x IF x

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `beats` b IF a AND NOT b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
a `reduced by` b MEANS a MINUS b

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg %x% doubled
`dbl` x MEANS 2 * x

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %x% is due
`due` x MEANS x > 0

-- 1. Holes.

GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `one` x q r IF `shown` ((x `beats` (`fb` q)) AND r)

GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `two` x q r IF `shown` (x `beats` (`fb` (q AND r)))

GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `beats then shown` p q r IF `shown` (p `beats` (q AND r))

GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `shown in a hole` p q r IF p `beats` (`shown` (q AND r))

GIVEN price IS A NUMBER
      discount IS A NUMBER
      rebate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sum then reduced` price discount rebate MEANS price PLUS (discount `reduced by` rebate)

GIVEN price IS A NUMBER
      discount IS A NUMBER
      rebate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reduced then sum` price discount rebate MEANS (price PLUS discount) `reduced by` rebate

-- 2. Clauses.

GIVETH A NUMBER
`record then minus` MEANS (RECORD `balance` IS 100) MINUS 3

GIVETH A NUMBER
`record of a minus` MEANS RECORD `balance` IS (100 MINUS 3)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`refuse then minus` MEANS (REFUSE "not yet") MINUS 3

GIVETH A NUMBER
`record doubled` MEANS `dbl` (RECORD `balance` IS 100)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`record of a double` MEANS RECORD `balance` IS (`dbl` 100)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`refuse doubled` MEANS `dbl` (REFUSE "not yet")

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every recall due` MEANS `due` (sum (RECALL ALL `balance`))

#EVAL (RECORD `balance` IS 100) MINUS 3
#EVAL RECORD `balance` IS (100 MINUS 3)
#EVAL `dbl` (RECORD `balance` IS 100)
#EVAL RECORD `balance` IS (`dbl` 100)
#EVAL (REFUSE "not yet") MINUS 3
#EVAL `dbl` (REFUSE "not yet")
